utcomes\nof the `s1`/`s2` separator branches in `tool_basename`.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `tool_basename` | No options; no `/` or `\\` (empty and non-empty strings) | [ ] |\n| 2 | `tool_basename` | No options; one or more `/`, no `\\` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `tool_basename` | No options; one or more `\\`, no `/` | [ ] |\n| 4 | `tool_basename` | No options; both separator types, last `/` occurs later | [ ] |\n| 5 | `tool_basename` | No options; both separator types, last `\\` occurs later | [ ] |\n\nFor every row, comparison includes the returned pointer offset, returned suffix\nbytes through the terminating NUL, and confirmation that the input buffer is\nunchanged.\n[package]\nname = \"driver\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[lib]\ncrate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\nname = \"driver\"\n\n[workspace]\n\n[dev-dependencies]\nlibloading = \"0.8\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
